<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= this.size() && role != null => this.get(index).equals(role);</code>

However, there seems to be a slight issue with the logic in the assert statement. The `add` method shifts elements to the right when inserting at a specific index, so the inserted role will actually be at the specified index after the insertion, but the original element at that index (if any) will be shifted to the right. Therefore, the correct assertion should check that the role at the specified index after the insertion is equal to the inserted role.

Here is the corrected assert statement:
<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= this.size() && role != null => this.get(index).equals(role);</code>

This is actually correct as per the method's behavior. The role is inserted at the specified index, and elements at and after that index are shifted to the right. So the role at the specified index after the insertion should indeed be equal to the inserted role.
--------------------
<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size()) && role != null => this.get(index).equals(role);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size()) && role != null => this.get(index).equals(role);</code>
--------------------
